c Random Instance of Urquhart's Problem for SAT (size=7).
c Like Hole, this problem as been proved to be exponential for resolution.
c N.B. : instance is unsatisfiable by construction.
c
c Come from the paper 'Hard Examples for Resolution'.
c        Source : Laurent Simon, simon@lri.fr. May 1999.
c
c n=7, so there is m^2=49 vertices in each part of the bipartite graph.
c Bases creations :
c   - a '1' charge is 'there must be an even number of negated vars'
c   - edges contains variables from which all subbases are constructed.
c vertex A0 :(charge=1), (edges=[93,79,111,183,219,12])
c vertex A1 :(charge=1), (edges=[229,136,12,47])
c vertex A2 :(charge=0), (edges=[26,31,47,6])
c vertex A3 :(charge=0), (edges=[55,143,216,66,154,6,232])
c vertex A4 :(charge=0), (edges=[14,134,168,232,80])
c vertex A5 :(charge=1), (edges=[158,121,178,80,57])
c vertex A6 :(charge=1), (edges=[5,56,197,171,57,141])
c vertex A7 :(charge=0), (edges=[28,58,188,220,141,139])
c vertex A8 :(charge=0), (edges=[27,32,139,3])
c vertex A9 :(charge=1), (edges=[21,3,18])
c vertex A10 :(charge=0), (edges=[181,18,184])
c vertex A11 :(charge=1), (edges=[13,7,184,165])
c vertex A12 :(charge=1), (edges=[228,116,165,161])
c vertex A13 :(charge=0), (edges=[73,49,237,210,53,161,179])
c vertex A14 :(charge=1), (edges=[127,135,51,204,179,74])
c vertex A15 :(charge=0), (edges=[42,90,101,35,43,74,148])
c vertex A16 :(charge=1), (edges=[50,148,107])
c vertex A17 :(charge=0), (edges=[85,152,107,98])
